---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = "April 8, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy for undividedallegiance.com, The Remnant newsletter, and Undivided Allegiance ad campaigns.">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-black">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <span class="text-red text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] block mb-6">Privacy</span>
        <h1 class="mb-6">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="divider mb-6"></div>
        <p class="text-muted-light text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          How Undivided Allegiance collects, uses, and protects your information. Last updated {lastUpdated}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="fade-in space-y-12 text-muted-light leading-relaxed">

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">Who We Are</h2>
          <p>
            Undivided Allegiance is the publishing and ministry work of Drew Reitzel, author of "You Can't Serve Two Masters." This privacy policy applies to undividedallegiance.com, the email newsletter "The Remnant," and any advertising we run on platforms like Meta (Facebook and Instagram).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">Information We Collect</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">We collect only the information we need to send you what you asked for, measure whether our content is reaching the right people, and respond when you contact us.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-3 list-disc pl-6">
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Email address.</span> Collected when you subscribe to The Remnant newsletter through our embedded signup form, which is hosted by Beehiiv. We use this to send you newsletter issues and occasional book updates.</li>
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Contact form submissions.</span> If you fill out our contact form, we receive your name, email, subject, and message so we can reply.</li>
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Site analytics and ad measurement.</span> We use the Meta Pixel to understand which pages people visit, which buttons they click, and whether visitors who came from a Facebook or Instagram ad eventually subscribed or pre-ordered the book. This data is anonymized and aggregated.</li>
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Standard server logs.</span> Our hosting provider records basic technical data such as IP address, browser type, and timestamps. We do not actively review these logs unless investigating abuse or a security incident.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-3 list-disc pl-6">
            <li>To deliver The Remnant newsletter to subscribers.</li>
            <li>To respond to messages you send through the contact form.</li>
            <li>To measure the performance of our ads and improve which audiences see them.</li>
            <li>To understand how visitors use the site so we can write content that serves them better.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4">We do not sell your information. We do not rent it. We do not share it with anyone except the service providers listed below who help us run the site, the newsletter, and the ads.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">Third-Party Services We Use</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-3 list-disc pl-6">
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Beehiiv</span> hosts the newsletter and processes subscriber email addresses. Beehiiv's privacy policy: <a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/privacy" class="text-red hover:text-red-light underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">beehiiv.com/privacy</a>.</li>
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Meta (Facebook and Instagram)</span> hosts our ad campaigns and provides the Meta Pixel for measurement. Meta's privacy policy: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" class="text-red hover:text-red-light underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">facebook.com/privacy/policy</a>.</li>
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Amazon</span> handles all book purchases. When you click a pre-order button, you leave our site and are subject to Amazon's privacy policy: <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=GX7NJQ4ZB8MHFRNJ" class="text-red hover:text-red-light underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">amazon.com privacy notice</a>.</li>
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">GitHub Pages</span> serves the static website files.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">Cookies and Tracking</h2>
          <p>
            We use cookies set by the Meta Pixel to measure ad performance. You can disable advertising cookies through your browser settings or by adjusting your ad preferences directly with Meta at <a href="https://www.facebook.com/adpreferences" class="text-red hover:text-red-light underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">facebook.com/adpreferences</a>. We do not use cookies for any purpose other than measurement.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">Your Rights</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-3 list-disc pl-6">
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Unsubscribe at any time.</span> Every newsletter we send has an unsubscribe link at the bottom. One click removes you from the list.</li>
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Request deletion.</span> If you want us to remove your email or any contact form data we hold about you, email us using the address below and we will do so within 30 days.</li>
            <li><span class="text-cream font-semibold">Opt out of ad targeting.</span> Adjust your Meta ad preferences at the link above.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">Children</h2>
          <p>
            This site and our newsletter are not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has submitted information to us, please contact us and we will delete it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy as our publishing and advertising practices change. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be announced through The Remnant newsletter.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-cream mb-4">Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy, requests for data deletion, or anything else related to privacy can be sent to <a href="mailto:drew.reitzel@undividedallegiance.com" class="text-red hover:text-red-light underline">drew.reitzel@undividedallegiance.com</a>, or through the <a href="/contact/" class="text-red hover:text-red-light underline">contact form</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
